# Generative — 96 bpm, D dorian, one minute. A demo of generative
# automation lanes: `{expr}` segments that follow an expression of time,
# and the chaotic systems an expression can read.
#
#   beats  0-32   SWARM  three arpeggios panned by three voices of a
#                        Kuramoto swarm: the coupling rises through the
#                        section past the point where the swarm locks, and
#                        the voices go from scattered across the field to
#                        moving as one; the pad's cutoff rides the Lorenz
#                        attractor for the whole song
#   beats 32-64   MAP    a sixteenth-note line whose cutoff follows the
#                        logistic map, r stepping up every two bars: one
#                        value (r = 2.8), two alternating (3.2), a cycle of
#                        four (3.5), then chaos (3.9)
#   beats 64-96   FALL   a bell FM'd by a muted modulator, its index swung
#                        by a double pendulum, its reverb send from the
#                        Henon map; the tempo sags and recovers

bpm 96
gate 0.92
tail 3

section SWARM 0..32
section MAP 32..64
section FALL 64..96

automate reverb_wet
0.22
automate reverb_decay
0.75
automate bpm
96 R:64 {96 - 12 * sin(pi * p)}:32

# --- the bed: a pad on the Lorenz attractor, a drone bass on smooth noise
track pad patch=aurora vel=0.55 gain=0.8 reverb_send=0.35
([D3 F3 A3 C4]:8 [C3 E3 G3 B3]:8 [A#2 D3 F3 A3]:8 [C3 F3 A3 D4]:8)x3
automate pad.cutoff
{1800 + 1200 * lorenz(t / 3)}

track bass patch=deepsine vel=0.7 gain=0.7
(D2:8 C2:8 A#1:8 F1:8)x3
automate bass.cutoff
{500 + 300 * noise(b / 2, 7)}

# --- SWARM: three arpeggios, panned by three voices of one swarm
track arp1 patch=glintbell vel=0.6 gain=0.45 reverb_send=0.3
(D4:0.25 A4:0.25 F5:0.25 A4:0.25)x32
track arp2 patch=glintbell vel=0.55 gain=0.4 reverb_send=0.3
(F4:0.5 C5:0.5)x32
track arp3 patch=mallet vel=0.6 gain=0.45 reverb_send=0.3
(A4:0.75 D5:0.75 E5:0.5)x16
automate arp1.pan
{0.9 * kuramoto(t / 2, 10 * p, 1)}:32 0:2@smooth
automate arp2.pan
{0.9 * kuramoto(t / 2, 10 * p, 2)}:32 0:2@smooth
automate arp3.pan
{0.9 * kuramoto(t / 2, 10 * p, 3)}:32 0:2@smooth

# --- MAP: the logistic map's period doubling, one value per sixteenth
track line patch=acidline vel=0.75 gain=0.8 reverb_send=0.15
>MAP (D3:0.25 D3:0.25 D4:0.25 D3:0.25)x32
automate line.cutoff
400 >MAP {300 * 2 ^ (4 * logistic(s * 4, seq(s / 8, 2.8, 3.2, 3.5, 3.9)))}:32@4

# --- FALL: a bell FM'd by a muted modulator, swung by a double pendulum
track bellmod patch=deepsine gain=0
>FALL (A5:8 G5:8 F5:8 A5:8)
track bell patch=deepsine vel=0.75 gain=0.9 fm_from=bellmod fm=0
>FALL (D4:8 C4:8 A#3:8 D4:8)
automate bell.fm
0 >FALL {2.5 + 2 * pendulum(s / 3, 1)}:30 0:2@smooth
automate bell.reverb_send
0.3 >FALL {0.35 + 0.25 * henon(b * 2)}:32
